--- !u!114 &6475245448296321767
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2988461138595263597}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9f623ee2a26514a4d91aefdd3a055a6c, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  CanAutoPlay: 0
  Canvas: {fileID: 0}
  videoDataList:
  - time: 9
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Greetings, clever young geologists. My name is Marvin, and I'm
      a very fancy kind of golem. I'm quite different from all the others you've
      met so far.
  - time: 6
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Can you guess what type of rock I am made of? Let me give you
      a few clues.
  - time: 13
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Clue one. I'm super smooth and shiny. When I'm polished, I can
      gleam like a mirror. People think I'm one of the most beautiful rocks in the
      world.
  - time: 14
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Clue two. I'm often white or cream-colored, but I can have gorgeous
      swirls, veins, and ribbons of grey, pink, green, or even gold running through
      me. I look like nature's artwork.
  - time: 14
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Clue three. Here's something amazing. I used to be a completely
      different rock. I started life as my friend Leroy the Limestone, but then something
      incredible happened deep underground that changed me completely.
  - time: 13
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Clue four. Famous artists love to carve me into beautiful statues
      and sculptures because I'm smooth, strong, and gorgeous. Many of the world's
      most famous statues are made from rocks like me.
  - time: 7
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Have you guessed it yet? I'm made of marble. That's right, marble.
  - time: 12
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Now here's where things get really exciting. I'm neither an
      igneous rock like Barry and Gracie, nor a sedimentary rock like Leroy and Sally.
      I'm a metamorphic rock. That's a big word that means changed rock.
  - time: 27
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Let me explain. A long, long time ago, I was actually Leroy
      the Limestone. But then, deep underground, something incredible happened. The
      Earth's movements pushed and squeezed me, and it got super hot down there.
      Not hot enough to melt me completely, but hot enough to change me. All that
      heat and pressure cooked me and rearranged my crystals, transforming me from
      rough limestone into smooth, beautiful marble.
  - time: 14
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: It's like I went through a magical makeover deep inside the
      Earth. My stunning appearance. Usually white or cream-colored, like limestone
      used to be, but I often have beautiful colored veins, swirls, and ribbons running
      through me.
  - time: 20
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: These colorful patterns come from other minerals that got mixed
      in during my transformation. Pink veins from iron, green veins from serpentine
      minerals, gray veins from graphite. No two pieces of marble look exactly the
      same. I'm unique.
  - time: 23
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: My smooth texture. Because all that heat and pressure reorganized
      my crystals, I became smooth and fine-grained. When I'm polished, I can shine
      like glass. My crystals are interlocked, stuck together really tightly, which
      makes me smooth and beautiful. You can't feel individual grains like you can
      with Sally Sandstone.
  - time: 22
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: My strength? I'm harder and stronger than my old self, Leroy
      Limestone, but I'm still softer than igneous rocks like Gracie Granite. I'm
      perfect for carving because I'm hard enough to last for thousands of years,
      soft enough to carve into detailed sculptures, smooth enough to polish to a
      brilliant shine, my limestone secret.
  - time: 15
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Even though I've been transformed, I still have something in
      common with Leroy. I'm still made of calcium carbonate. That means if you put
      vinegar on me, I'll still fizz a little bit, just like limestone does.
  - time: 20
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Where you can find me? I'm found in places where limestone was
      buried deep underground and got cooked by heat and pressure, mountain ranges
      where rocks were squeezed together, deep underground where it's hot, places
      where tectonic plates have pushed rocks together.
  - time: 30
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: What makes me so special to humans? Sculptures. Some of the
      world's most famous statues are carved from marble. Michelangelo's David, the
      Parthenon in Greece, and many other masterpieces. Buildings. Fancy buildings,
      palaces, and monuments are made with marble, floors and countertops. My polished
      surface is beautiful in homes, tombstones, and memorials. I last for hundreds
      of years, even outside.
  - time: 23
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Decorations. People love my natural beauty for decorative items.
      Famous marble facts. The Taj Mahal in India is covered in white marble. Many
      ancient Greek and Roman statues were carved from marble. The Lincoln Memorial
      in Washington, D.C. is made of marble. Carrara marble from Italy is one of
      the most famous types in the world.
  - time: 32
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Cool fact about metamorphic rocks. Being metamorphic means I
      was changed. Meta means change, and morph means form. So I changed my form.
      Heat and pressure deep underground can change lots of rocks. Limestone becomes
      marble. That's me. Sandstone becomes quartzite. Shale becomes slate. It's like
      rocks going through a transformation deep inside the earth.
  - time: 27
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: So remember, young geologists, I'm Marvin the Marble Golem,
      born when limestone was cooked by heat and pressure deep underground, smooth
      and beautiful, perfect for sculptures. I'm a metamorphic rock, which means
      I'm a changed rock with a special story. Isn't it amazing? I started out as
      Leroy Limestone, but the earth's powerful forces transformed me into something
      completely new.
  - time: 27
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: That's the magic of metamorphic rocks. We show you that rocks
      aren't just rocks. They can change over millions of years. Now you've met igneous
      rocks from heat and melting, sedimentary rocks from layers and squashing, and
      metamorphic rocks from changing under heat and pressure. You're becoming real
      rock experts. Who will you meet next on your explorations?
  displayImage: {fileID: 0}
  displayText: {fileID: 0}
  SubtitleCanvas: {fileID: 0}
  animator: {fileID: 5470954140284980469}
  audioSource: {fileID: 553416498008168658}
  AmbiantAudioSource: {fileID: 0}
  TalkingAnim:
  - {fileID: -203655887218126122, guid: 0e9551bc6cd60f04d97113009568c675, type: 3}
  - {fileID: -203655887218126122, guid: 5fee6e4c39a7c8548a4aad93d5ef8a21, type: 3}
  - {fileID: -203655887218126122, guid: 0d557617e530e3b4293fc607895e85e0, type: 3}
  IdleState: Idle
