--- !u!114 &7782418512471565807
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 4381550666326819795}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9f623ee2a26514a4d91aefdd3a055a6c, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  CanAutoPlay: 0
  Canvas: {fileID: 0}
  videoDataList:
  - time: 13
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Hello, wonderful rock explorers. My name is Gracie, and I'm
      a very beautiful kind of golem, if I do say so myself. Can you guess what type
      of rock I am made of? Let me give you a few clues.
  - time: 12
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Clue 1. I'm much lighter in color than my friend Barry the basalt.
      I can be pink, gray, white, or even a mix of all these colors. I look much
      brighter than him.
  - time: 14
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Clue 2. Look closely at me. Do you see all those sparkly speckles
      and spots? I'm like a rocky rainbow. You can see lots of different colored
      crystals all over me without even using a magnifying glass.
  - time: 17
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Clue 3. Like Barry, I'm also born from melted rock. But I was
      made deep underground, not from a volcano. The melted rock cooled down very,
      very slowly under the Earth, and that's what made me so sparkly.
  - time: 15.5
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Clue 4. I'm super strong and tough. Humans love to use rocks
      like me for kitchen benchtops, fancy buildings, and monuments because I last
      for hundreds and hundreds of years. Have you figured it out yet? I'm made of
      granite.
  - time: 12.5
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: That's right, granite. Just like Barry, I'm an igneous rock,
      made from hot, melted rock that cooled down. But here's the exciting difference.
  - time: 24
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: While Barry was made from lava on top of the Earth, I was made
      from something called magma deep under the Earth. Here's what makes me special,
      where I come from. Deep, deep underground, there's hot, melted rock called
      magma. When this magma gets trapped under the Earth's surface, it cools down
      very slowly over thousands and thousands of years, and that makes me granite,
  - time: 18
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: my amazing colors. I'm usually light-colored, pink, gray, white,
      or cream. But the best part? I'm made of lots of different colored minerals
      all mixed together, which makes me look speckled and beautiful, my sparkly
      crystals.
  - time: 12.5
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Because I cooled down so slowly deep underground, my crystals
      had lots of time to grow big. You can see them easily with your own eyes. I
      have three main types of crystals.
  - time: 13
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Quartz, usually clear or milky white and very shiny. Feldspar,
      often pink, white, or gray. Mica, the super sparkly black or silver flecks
      that catch the light.
  - time: 10
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: My texture. I feel bumpy and rough because of all my big crystals.
      Run your hand over granite sometime. Can you feel all those different bits?
  - time: 10
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: My strength. I'm one of the hardest rocks around. I'm so strong
      that I can last for thousands of years, even in rain, wind, and sun.
  - time: 18
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: That's why I'm perfect for building. Where you can find me.
      I'm found all over the world. Mountains are often made of granite, and humans
      use me for buildings, bridges, monuments, and even kitchen countertops. You
      might have granite in your home.
  - time: 14
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Cool fact. Because I formed deep underground, the only way you
      can see me now is if the rocks above me wore away over millions of years, or
      if mountains pushed me up to the surface.
  - time: 26
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: So remember, young geologists, I'm Gracie the Granite Golem,
      born deep underground, sparkly and strong, with big beautiful crystals you
      can see. Aren't igneous rocks fascinating? Barry and I are both igneous, but
      we look so different because of where and how fast we cool down. You should
      find more of my rocky friends down here. They are so eager to meet you
  displayImage: {fileID: 0}
  displayText: {fileID: 0}
  SubtitleCanvas: {fileID: 0}
  animator: {fileID: 7275925486088263175}
  audioSource: {fileID: 2453221930182519841}
  AmbiantAudioSource: {fileID: 0}
  TalkingAnim:
  - {fileID: -203655887218126122, guid: 0e9551bc6cd60f04d97113009568c675, type: 3}
  - {fileID: -203655887218126122, guid: 5fee6e4c39a7c8548a4aad93d5ef8a21, type: 3}
  - {fileID: -203655887218126122, guid: 0d557617e530e3b4293fc607895e85e0, type: 3}
  IdleState: Idle
  WaveState: Wave
  TalkingState: Talking
  WaveDuration: 2
