--- !u!114 &4704658992688400378
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 6654974095370080414}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9f623ee2a26514a4d91aefdd3a055a6c, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  CanAutoPlay: 0
  Canvas: {fileID: 0}
  videoDataList:
  - time: 6
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Hello there, young explorers. My name is Barry, and I'm a very
      special kind of golem.
  - time: 5
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Can you guess what type of rock I am made of? Let me give you
      a few clues.
  - time: 10
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Clue 1. I'm usually very dark in color. Sometimes black, sometimes
      dark gray. Look closely at me. What color do you see?
  - time: 14
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Clue 2. I was born from a volcano. A long, long time ago, hot,
      melted rock called lava flowed out of a volcano, and when it cooled down really
      quickly, it made... me.
  - time: 10
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Clue 3. If you could touch my surface, you'd feel that I'm very
      smooth and my crystals are super tiny. So tiny you might need a magnifying
      glass to see them properly.
  - time: 7
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: That's because I cool down so fast. Clue 4. Sometimes I have
      little holes all over me, like a sponge.
  - time: 12
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: These holes were made by gas bubbles trapped inside the lava
      when it was cooling down. Have you guessed yet? I'm made of basalt. That's
      right, bay salt.
  - time: 14
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: I'm what scientists call an igneous rock. That's a fancy word
      that means I was made from hot, melted rock that cooled down and became solid.
      Igneous comes from a word that means fire. Pretty cool, right?
  - time: 6
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Here's what makes me special. Where I come from. I was born
      in a volcano.
  - time: 9
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: When lava flows out of a volcano and touches the cool air or
      water, it cools down super fast. And that makes basalt.
  - time: 7
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: My color. I'm usually dark, black, dark gray, or sometimes dark
      brown.va flows out of a volcano and touches the cool air or water, it cools
      down super fast. And that makes basalt.
  - time: 9
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: This is because I have lots of dark minerals inside me. My texture.
      I feel smooth because my crystals are really, really small.
  - time: 5
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: They're so small because I cool down too quickly for big crystals
      to grow.
  - time: 8
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: My strength. I'm super strong and hard. That's why humans use
      rocks like me to build roads and buildings.
  - time: 7
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: My holes. Sometimes I have little holes called vesicles. Say
      it. Ves-e-cules.
  - time: 6
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: These were made by gas bubbles in the lava, like bubbles in
      your bath.
  - time: 10
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Where you can find me. I'm one of the most common rocks on Earth.
      You can find me near volcanoes, and I even cover most of the ocean floor.
  - time: 5
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: In fact, the dark areas you see on the moon are made of basalt
      too. It's true.
  - time: 5
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: In fact, the dark areas you see on the moon are made of basalt
      too. It's true.
  - time: 14
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: The dark areas on the moon, called maria, Latin for seas, are
      vast plains of solidified basalt lava, rich in iron and magnesium, which makes
      them darker and less reflective than the lighter, older highland crust.
  - time: 11
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: So remember, young geologists, I'm Barry the Basalt Golem, born
      from volcanic lava, dark and strong, and ready to teach you all about igneous
      rocks.
  displayImage: {fileID: 0}
  displayText: {fileID: 0}
  SubtitleCanvas: {fileID: 0}
  animator: {fileID: 2468681405841669237}
  audioSource: {fileID: 7553975255725565956}
  AmbiantAudioSource: {fileID: 0}
  TalkingAnim:
  - {fileID: -203655887218126122, guid: 0e9551bc6cd60f04d97113009568c675, type: 3}
  - {fileID: -203655887218126122, guid: 5fee6e4c39a7c8548a4aad93d5ef8a21, type: 3}
  - {fileID: -203655887218126122, guid: 0d557617e530e3b4293fc607895e85e0, type: 3}
  IdleState: Idle
  WaveState: Wave
  TalkingState: Talking
  WaveDuration: 2
