--- !u!114 &7664413947583415065
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 6983106547330724187}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9f623ee2a26514a4d91aefdd3a055a6c, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  CanAutoPlay: 0
  Canvas: {fileID: 0}
  videoDataList:
  - time: 13
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Hello, wonderful rock detectives. My name is Quinn, and I'm
      a very special kind of golem. Actually, I'm a bit different from all the others
      you've met. Can you guess what I'm made of? Let me give you a few clues.
  - time: 15
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Clue 1. I'm often crystal clear, like glass or ice, but I can
      also be white, pink, purple, yellow, or even smoky gray. Sometimes I'm so see-through
      you can look right through me.
  - time: 10
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Clue 2. I'm super hard, one of the hardest natural things you
      can find. I'm much harder than all the rock golems you've met so far. I can
      scratch glass.
  - time: 12
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Clue 3. I often grow in beautiful pointy crystal shapes with
      six sides. When I form perfectly, I look like a magical crystal wand.
  - time: 16
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Clue 4. Here's my big secret. I'm not actually a rock like Barry,
      Gracie, Leroy, Sally, and Marvin. I'm something called a mineral, and you can
      find me hiding inside many different rocks. Have you figured it out? I'm made
      of quartz.
  - time: 5
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: That's right, quartz. Now, here's something really important
      to understand. I'm a mineral, not a rock.
  - time: 23
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Let me explain the difference in a simple way. What's the difference
      between rocks and minerals? Think of it like this. Minerals are like the ingredients.
      Single, pure substances with their own special recipe. Rocks are like cakes
      or cookies, made by mixing different mineral ingredients together. So I'm an
      ingredient that helps make rocks.
  - time: 15
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: In fact, you've already seen me before. Remember Gracie the
      granite golem? Those clear, glassy bits in her are me, quartz crystals. Remember
      Sally the sandstone golem? She's made of sand, and most sand is actually tiny
      pieces of me, broken down over time.
  - time: 17
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: What I'm made of. I'm made of two elements, the building blocks
      of everything. Silicon, say it, silicon, oxygen. These combine to make silicon
      dioxide. That's my scientific name. I'm actually one of the most common minerals
      on Earth.
  - time: 27
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: My amazing colors. Even though I'm often clear or white, I can
      be lots of beautiful colors. Clear quartz, like glass or ice, also called rock
      crystal. Purple quartz, called amethyst, a precious gemstone. Pink quartz,
      called rose quartz. Yellow quartz, called citrine. Smoky quartz, gray or brown
      colored. Milky quartz, cloudy white. The different colors come from tiny amounts
      of other minerals mixed in with me.
  - time: 12
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: My crystal shape. When I have room to grow properly, I form
      beautiful six-sided crystals with pointed ends, like a magical wand. These
      are called hexagonal crystals.
  - time: 27
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Some quartz crystals can grow to be huge, even taller than a
      person. My super hardness. I'm rated 7 on something called the Mohs hardness
      scale. That's how scientists measure how hard minerals are. That means I can
      scratch glass. I can scratch steel. I'm harder than all the rock golems you've
      met. Only a few things are harder than me, like diamonds. This hardness makes
      me very special and useful.
  - time: 12
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: My shine. When I'm broken or polished, I have a glassy shine.
      Scientists call this vitreous luster, which just means I shine like glass,
      where you can find me.
  - time: 23
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: I'm everywhere. I'm one of the most common minerals on planet
      Earth. Inside granite rocks, like Gracie, making up most sand, the stuff Sally
      is made from. In beautiful crystal caves, in veins running through other rocks,
      on beaches, most sand is broken down quartz, in deserts, in riverbeds.
  - time: 38
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: What humans use me for. Because I'm so hard and special, humans
      use me for lots of things. Watches and clocks. I vibrate in a very precise
      way, which helps keep perfect time. Electronics. I'm in computers, phones,
      and radios. Jewelry, purple amethyst, and pink rose quartz make beautiful gems.
      Glassmaking. I'm melted down to help make glass. Sandpaper. Crushed quartz
      makes things rough for sanding. Buildings. I'm in concrete and many building
      materials. Countertops. Crushed quartz is mixed with resin to make kitchen
      counters.
  - time: 21
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: My special properties. Here are some cool things about me. Piezoelectric.
      When you squeeze me, I make a tiny bit of electricity. This is how quartz watches
      work. Tough. I don't break or wear down easily. Pure. I'm usually very pure
      silicon dioxide with few impurities. Common. I'm found all over the world in
      huge amounts.
  - time: 18
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Cool fact. The sand on most beaches is made of tiny pieces of
      me. Over millions of years, rocks like granite wear down, and the quartz crystals
      inside them break into tiny grains. Because I'm so hard, I last much longer
      than the other minerals, so I end up being most of the sand.
  - time: 14
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Another cool fact. Some cultures believed quartz crystals had
      magical powers. Clear quartz was called rock crystal, and people thought it
      was ice that had frozen so hard it would never melt.
  - time: 18
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: How I'm different from rocks. Let me explain again, because
      this is important. Berry, basalt, is a rock made of several different minerals
      mixed together. Gracie, granite, is a rock made of me, quartz, plus feldspar,
      plus mica, three minerals. Sally, sandstone, is a rock made of tiny pieces
      of me stuck together.
  - time: 13
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Me, Quinn, I'm just one mineral, pure quartz. So you can find
      me. As pure crystals in caves and rock veins, as one of the ingredients inside
      rocks like granite, as broken down pieces making sand and sandstone.
  - time: 20
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: So remember, young geologists, I'm Quinn the Quartz Golem, but
      I'm actually a mineral, not a rock. I'm one of the most common and useful minerals
      on Earth, super hard and sparkly, found in many different rocks, and I help
      make everything from watches to glass to beautiful gemstones. Now you know
      the difference between rocks and minerals.
  - time: 11
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Rocks are like mixtures made of different minerals, and minerals
      are the pure ingredients. I'm one of the most important mineral ingredients
      on Earth, and I'm hiding in lots of the rocks all around you. Learning about
      minerals helps you understand rocks even better.
  - time: 8
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Isn't geology amazing? Would you like to meet more golems and
      learn about other types of rocks or minerals?
  displayImage: {fileID: 0}
  displayText: {fileID: 0}
  SubtitleCanvas: {fileID: 0}
  animator: {fileID: 5018818662185946750}
  audioSource: {fileID: 5150898782486982789}
  AmbiantAudioSource: {fileID: 0}
  TalkingAnim:
  - {fileID: -203655887218126122, guid: 0e9551bc6cd60f04d97113009568c675, type: 3}
  - {fileID: -203655887218126122, guid: 5fee6e4c39a7c8548a4aad93d5ef8a21, type: 3}
  - {fileID: -203655887218126122, guid: 0d557617e530e3b4293fc607895e85e0, type: 3}
  IdleState: Idle
  WaveState: Wave
  TalkingState: Talking
  WaveDuration: 2
