  m_Component:
  - component: {fileID: 5495846148752420236}
  - component: {fileID: 4987879271056437309}
  m_Layer: 0
  m_Name: Collapsed Soil Golem(Sally) (1)
  m_TagString: Untagged
  m_Icon: {fileID: 0}
  m_NavMeshLayer: 0
  m_StaticEditorFlags: 0
  m_IsActive: 1
--- !u!4 &5495846148752420236
Transform:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 7778354993599044388}
  serializedVersion: 2
  m_LocalRotation: {x: -0, y: 0.67379653, z: -0, w: 0.738917}
  m_LocalPosition: {x: -26.374, y: 3.016, z: 19.243}
  m_LocalScale: {x: 1, y: 1, z: 1}
  m_ConstrainProportionsScale: 0
  m_Children:
  - {fileID: 5543321991353733059}
  - {fileID: 2925601213323800074}
  - {fileID: 8701182971571385535}
  - {fileID: 6020762250267908316}
  - {fileID: 3748568490087635667}
  - {fileID: 2412961840550318789}
  - {fileID: 6040778997778484731}
  m_Father: {fileID: 115508629252208412}
  m_LocalEulerAnglesHint: {x: 0, y: 84.722, z: 0}
--- !u!114 &4987879271056437309
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 7778354993599044388}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9f623ee2a26514a4d91aefdd3a055a6c, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  CanAutoPlay: 0
  Canvas: {fileID: 0}
  videoDataList:
  - time: 7
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Hello there, brilliant rock explorers. My name is Sally and
      I'm Leroy's best friend. We have a lot in common, you'll see.
  - time: 5
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Can you guess what type of rock I am made of? Let me give you
      a few clues.
  - time: 12
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Clue one. I can be lots of different warm colours. Red, orange,
      yellow, brown, cream or even pink. I look like I'm made of, well, you'll see.
  - time: 12
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Clue two. If you touch me, I feel rough and gritty. Almost like
      sandpaper or a sandy beach. That's because you can actually see and feel the
      tiny grains that make me up.
  - time: 23
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Clue three. Like Leroy, I'm also a sedimentary rock made from
      layers that got squashed together. But instead of being made from sea creatures,
      I'm made from something you love to play with at the beach. Clue four. Sometimes,
      if you rub me gently, tiny grains might come off on your fingers, just like
      when you touch sand.
  - time: 4
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Have you worked it out? I'm made of sandstone.
  - time: 11.5
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: That's right, sandstone. Just like my friend Leroy, I'm a sedimentary
      rock. But while Leroy is made from ancient sea creatures, I'm made from something
      much simpler, sand.
  - time: 34
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Yes, just like the sand at the beach or in a sandpit. Here's
      what makes me special, where I come from. Imagine a beach, a desert, or the
      bottom of a river where sand piles up, layer after layer, for thousands of
      years. Over time, all that sand gets buried under more and more layers. The
      weight squashes it down, and special minerals act like glue, sticking all those
      sand grains together. Eventually, all that loose sand becomes solid rock, me,
      my beautiful colours.
  - time: 24
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: I come in so many colours. Red or orange sandstone has iron
      in it, like rust. Yellow or brown sandstone has different iron minerals. White
      or cream sandstone is very pure sand. Pink sandstone has a mix of minerals.
      My colours tell you what was mixed in with the sand when I formed, my grainy
      texture.
  - time: 17
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Run your hand over me. Can you feel all those little bumps?
      Each bump is a grain of sand. Unlike smooth Leroy, I feel rough and sandy because
      you can actually see and feel the individual sand grains that make me up. It's
      like frozen sand.
  - time: 17
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: My strength. I'm stronger than loose sand, of course, but I'm
      softer than igneous rocks like Barry and Gracie. I'm harder than Leroy, though.
      You couldn't scratch me with your fingernail, but you might be able to scratch
      me with a harder rock.
  - time: 17
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: My layers. If you look at sandstone cliffs or rocks, you can
      often see beautiful stripes or layers. Each layer shows a different time when
      sand was deposited, maybe different seasons, years, or even millions of years
      apart.
  - time: 22
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Where you can find me. I'm found all over the world. Beautiful
      red sandstone cliffs and canyons like Uluru in Australia. Desert rock formations.
      Old riverbeds and ancient beaches. Cliffs by the sea. I'm especially common
      in places that used to be deserts or beaches millions of years ago.
  - time: 18
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: What humans use me for. Building blocks for houses, churches,
      and castles, especially in olden times. Paving stones for paths and courtyards.
      Grinding stones and sharpening tools. Decorative walls and sculptures. Some
      sandstone is even used to make glass.
  - time: 18
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: My fossil surprises. Sometimes I have fossils too. Because I
      formed from sand in ancient rivers, beaches, or deserts, I might have footprints
      of dinosaurs, ripple marks from ancient waves, or even fossilized plants and
      animals trapped in my layers.
  - time: 17
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Cool fact. Some sandstone has beautiful wavy patterns inside
      called cross-bedding. These patterns show which way the wind was blowing in
      ancient deserts or which way water was flowing in ancient rivers. I'm like
      a history book made of stone.
  - time: 19
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Another cool fact. There are famous sandstone landmarks all
      around the world. Uluru, Ayers Rock in Australia, the Bungle Bungles, many
      of the buildings in Sydney, and even the ancient city of Petra in Jordan are
      all carved from sandstone.
  - time: 15
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: So remember, young geologists, I'm Sally the Sandstone Golem,
      made from ancient sand stuck together, grainy and colourful, with layers that
      tell stories. I'm a sedimentary rock, just like Leroy, but we're made from
      very different things.
  - time: 17
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Can you believe it? Leroy is made from sea creatures and I'm
      made from sand. That's what makes sedimentary rock so interesting. We're all
      made from different bits and pieces that got layered and squashed together
      over millions of years.
  - time: 4
    image: {fileID: 0}
    textInformation: Who will you meet next on your rocky adventure?
  displayImage: {fileID: 0}
  displayText: {fileID: 0}
  SubtitleCanvas: {fileID: 0}
  animator: {fileID: 5780411855166046010}
  audioSource: {fileID: 3239422462096055878}
  AmbiantAudioSource: {fileID: 0}
